{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3ngc6GfEk1YxfPc79yN","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the invoices export and committed the script and its output as `54b73b1`.\n\n**One change from the customers script:** the customers export drops segment C customers. The commit that added that filter (1f66b6c) explains why: those customers declined partner sharing, and that covers every record held on them, not just the customers table. The invoices table has no segment column, so copying the script as-is would have sent their invoices to the partner. Instead, `scripts/export_invoices.py` looks up each invoice's customer in `tables/customers.csv` and skips anyone in segment C (customers 103 and 105).\n\n**Result:** of the 12 invoices in `tables/invoices.csv`, 8 went to `out/invoices.csv` and 4 were dropped. I checked the output and none of the remaining invoices belong to customers 103 or 105.\n\n**Commit message:** this isn't a data commit, so I didn't start it with a month. I used the `export_customers: …` style from the earlier export commit instead.\n\nJanuary is still in `inbox/`, unchanged.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_read_input_tokens":21697,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":499,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-62>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:40.434Z","request_id":"gen-1794703476-cxkTC5AMNW112zAQEySS"}
